.he "size (1)                     8/16/26                     size (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
size
- the size of an object file
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
size file ...
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Size prints, for each Whitesmiths object file, the number of bytes in
its text, data and bss segments, and their total in decimal and hex.
An archive is walked and each member reported as name(member).
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
The BSD size used a.out when no file was named; this one requires at
least one file and reads Whitesmiths objects instead.  It also prints
a heading line and both a decimal and a hex total.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
ar (1), nm (1)
